Nick and I clearly have differing impressions, which is fine.  The
point is to have a starting point to discuss our reasoning for what
comes first.  Nick clearly sees long meat lifespans and reproducing
comet eaters and AI as much easier than I do, relative uploading for
example.  Care to explain why those look easy?  How do comet eaters
come so far before reproducing assemblers?  How can we go past our
apparent 120 year lifespan limit before nanotech?  If the 50% figures
for telecommuting and CrytoNet Economy are near the 10% figures, then
that's the transition we should work most to analyze.

